From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:25:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 115/125] feat(refinery): run gates and classify reds through
 known-red (gcp-jb9f)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gc-cgxps phase 2, part 3: the refinery side of what gcp-oczc did for the
polecat. The refinery filed base reds with a title-keyword gc bd search and
a hand-written create. Those beads carry no failure ids, so neither
known-red nor a polecat could match them, and one red became several beads.

run-tests now runs setup/typecheck/lint/build/test through gate_run (an
identical copy of oczc's gate-run block), each gate named after its formula
var, into one truncated log at <git-dir>/refinery-gate.log. Every gate still
runs after one FAILs. handle-failures gains a step 0 that resolves the
pack's known-red for mol-refinery-patrol (an identical resolve-known-red
copy) and runs `known-red match` on that log. Only exit 0 (every red KNOWN)
merges past, with a note on the work bead. Exits 1 and 3 list the NEW and
FIXED-UPSTREAM rows for diagnosis. Exit 3 is diagnosed here, not merged
past: HEAD is already rebased onto the target, so a missing fix commit is
missing from the target itself. Step 0 hands the resolved path to §3
through <git-dir>/refinery-known-red.path, because §3 runs in a later
fence. §3 files through `known-red file` first. It nudges the witness when
a closed bead's red reproduces, and it fails closed (mayor escalation,
witness nudge, drain-ack, exit 1) when file errors. The DUP_KEYWORD block
is kept byte-for-byte for raw-only reds and for the no-known-red case.

One deviation from the brief: the FIXED-UPSTREAM witness nudge also fires
at file exit 1, not only exit 0, because known-red prints the fixed-upstream
lines before it returns 1 for raw lines.

Validation: test_known_red_wiring.sh gains (f2) structure/copy identity,
(g) refinery-gates, (h) match and (i) file. Against e585cda6's formulas,
(f2), (g), (h) and (i) fail while (a)-(f) pass. Ten formula mutations each
turn the suite red: exit 3 treated as known, no truncation, lint renamed,
stop after FAIL, no nudge, escalation exits 0, gate-run drift, resolving
the polecat formula, no path file, run_tests ignored. All 18
gastown/tests/*.sh exit 0. The drift test passes. pytest tests/ is
1F/170P/7S, and the one failure is gcp-98gh (known).

